# Description:
# ------------
# The ncpu script prints the number of CPU cores. It provides a portable,
# POSIX-compliant method to dynamically determine this count across different
# UNIX-like operating systems.
#
# This script provides a portable, POSIX-compliant method to dynamically
# determine the number of available CPU cores across different UNIX-like
# operating systems.
#
# Key features of this implementation:
#
# - Support Linux, macOS, BSD, and Solaris environments (getconf, nproc, and
#   sysctl).
# - If all hardware checks fail or are missing, it safely falls back to 1 to
#   prevent syntax errors in downstream commands.
# - It avoids Bash-specific syntax, ensuring it runs reliably in minimal shell
#   environments like dash or standard /bin/sh.
# - It redirects standard error to /dev/null to prevent terminal pollution if a
#   specific tool is not installed on the host system.
